  "submission": {
    "github_username": "mcknightconsulting",
    "description": "Independent TPROC-C test of MariaDB Enterprise Server 12.3.3 by McKnight Consulting Group, sponsored by MariaDB. The goal was to measure how far the database engine scales across a high core count, so the run is CPU-intensive: the 768-warehouse schema fits entirely in a 256 GB buffer pool and commits are non-durable, which takes disk I/O off the critical path.\n\nHardware: Google Cloud c4d-highmem-192-lssd (us-east1-b), AMD EPYC 9B45 (Turin), 1 socket, 96 cores, SMT on (192 vCPU), single NUMA node, 1.5 TB RAM. Storage: 16 x 375 GB Local SSD in mdadm RAID 0, ext4. Ubuntu 24.04.5, kernel 7.0. HammerDB ran on the same VM over a Unix socket.\n\nWorkload: 768 warehouses, stored procedures, no keying/thinking time, Use All Warehouses off, 2 min ramp-up + 5 min timed. This job is the 152-VU point of a ladder (64-216 VU) and was the peak. The buffer pool was flushed clean before each point.\n\nTuning versus a stock config: innodb_io_capacity 5000 / io_capacity_max 40000, max_dirty_pages_pct 90 / lwm 0, adaptive_flushing_lwm 10, purge_threads 32 / purge_batch_size 5000, innodb_deadlock_detect OFF (true deadlocks resolve via the 50 s lock wait timeout), thread pool (pool-of-threads, size 192).",
    "company": {
      "name": "McKnight Consulting Group",
      "logo_url": "https://mcknightcg.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/mcknight-logo.png",
      "description": "An independent data and AI consultancy specializing in enterprise data strategy, architecture, performance benchmarking, and business-driven technology transformation"
    },
    "workload": {
      "classification": "cpu-intensive",
      "use_all_warehouses": false,
      "durability": "relaxed",
      "details": "innodb_flush_log_at_trx_commit=0; skip_log_bin=1 (no binary log, sync_binlog n/a); innodb_doublewrite=0; innodb_buffer_pool_size=256G with innodb_log_file_size=64G (768-warehouse schema fully cached); Use All Warehouses disabled. Other: innodb_io_capacity=5000, innodb_io_capacity_max=40000, innodb_max_dirty_pages_pct=90, innodb_max_dirty_pages_pct_lwm=0, innodb_adaptive_flushing_lwm=10, innodb_purge_threads=32, innodb_purge_batch_size=5000, innodb_deadlock_detect=OFF, thread_handling=pool-of-threads, table_open_cache_instances=31, innodb_adaptive_hash_index=0, performance_schema=OFF."
    }
  }
